<title>GERMANY: East German Dec adjusted unemployment rises 26,000.</title>
<headline>East German Dec adjusted unemployment rises 26,000.</headline>
<dateline>NUREMBERG, Germany 1997-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Labour Office reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p> E.GERMAN UNEMPLOYMENT   Dec 96	 Nov 96	   Dec 95</p>
<p> Number (unadj)	    1.186 mln    1.117 mln	1.113 mln</p>
<p> Number (adj)		1.208 mln    1.182 mln	1.139 mln</p>
<p> Change (adj)	     +26,000	+23,000	   n/a</p>
<p> Rate (unadj)		15.9 pct     15.0 pct	 14.9 pct</p>
<p> Short-time workers	46,788	 44,489	   64,357</p>
<p> Vacancies		   48,923	 56,825	   44,770</p>
<p> Change in number in work Oct 96	Sept 96</p>
<p>				 -4,000	 -9,000</p>
<p>NOTE - Numbers in work data refer to change from previous month. Details on numbers in work to be released later today. --Bonn newsroom, 49-228-609750</p>
</text>
